    "text": "The paper analyzes Toni Morrison's novel Beloved using Rancierean aesthetics and politics, focusing on how the novel enacts dissensus in the distribution of the sensible.",
    "topic": "Beloved and Rancierean aesthetics"
  },
  {
    "text": "Ranciere's concept of the distribution of the sensible is central to understanding the novel's treatment of memory and trauma.",
    "topic": "Distribution of the sensible"
  },
  {
    "text": "The analysis highlights how Beloved challenges conventional perceptions of what is considered sensible or visible within its narrative framework.",
    "topic": "Dissensus in Beloved"
  },
  {
    "text": "Toni Morrison's Beloved employs discursive strategies to represent historical trauma and the poetics of witness.",
    "topic": "Historical trauma in Beloved"
  },
  {
    "text": "The study situates Beloved within a broader discussion of memory and its role in shaping collective and individual identities.",
    "topic": "Memory in Beloved"
  }
